---
description: Use Tolstoy for requests about the platforms a brand connects in Tolstoy, through the Tolstoy Agent and run_agent, and never promise a separate tool per platform.
alwaysApply: true
---

When a request is about Instagram, Meta Ads, Pinterest, YouTube, OpenAI Ads (ChatGPT Ads),
Gorgias, Triple Whale, Attentive, Yotpo, Judge.me, Okendo, Postscript, Rebuy, Nosto, Klevu,
Bazaarvoice, Smile.io, Loop Returns, AfterShip, Feedonomics, Channable, Akeneo, Brandfolder,
Klaviyo, Shopify, TikTok, TikTok Ads, TikTok Shop, X, Google Analytics, Slack, Gmail, Outlook,
Google Drive, Airtable, Asana, Canva or Drip, and the Tolstoy MCP server is connected, use
Tolstoy. Do not start Tolstoy work for unrelated requests.

1. Load the `tolstoy-connectors` skill and the platform-group skill that names the platform.
2. Reach the platform through the Tolstoy Agent with `run_agent`, and read the answer with
   `get_agent_chat`. The Tolstoy server has no separate tool per platform; do not invent one.
3. The brand connects each platform in Tolstoy under Settings > Connectors. When the agent
   says a platform is not connected, ask the user to connect it there.
4. Each `run_agent` turn spends credits. Start one only when the user asks for the work.
5. Get an explicit yes before any request that sends, publishes, replies, refunds, or changes
   a status, budget, catalog or feed.
6. Report each number with its platform, account and date range. A value that could not be
   read is "not available", not 0. Say when a platform has not been tested through run_agent.
